{
  "id": "26962_kikomu",
  "headword": "{着込|きこ}む",
  "reading": "きこむ",
  "romaji": "kikomu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb-godan",
  "gloss": "to bundle up; to put on many layers",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to put on many layers of clothing; to bundle up; to dress warmly",
      "explanation": "To wear multiple layers of clothing, typically for warmth. Often implies dressing more heavily than usual in response to cold weather."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "26962_kikomu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{厚|あつ}く{着込|きこ}む。",
      "english": "To bundle up warmly.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26962_kikomu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{今日|きょう}は{寒|さむ}いからたくさん{着込|きこ}んだ。",
      "english": "I bundled up because it's cold today.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26962_kikomu_ex3",
      "japanese": "セーターの{上|うえ}にコートまで{着込|きこ}んで{出|で}かけた。",
      "english": "I put on a coat over my sweater and went out.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26962_kikomu_ex4",
      "japanese": "{子供|こども}たちは{何枚|なんまい}も{着込|きこ}んで{雪遊|ゆきあそ}びに{出|で}かけた。",
      "english": "The children bundled up in many layers and went out to play in the snow.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Compound of {着|き}る (to wear) and {込|こ}む (suffix indicating thoroughness or accumulation). The {込|こ}む adds the nuance of putting on clothes in abundance or layers.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {厚|あつ}く{着込|きこ}む: to dress in thick layers\n- たくさん{着込|きこ}む: to put on lots of layers\n- {何枚|なんまい}も{着込|きこ}む: to wear many layers\n- しっかり{着込|きこ}む: to bundle up properly\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {重|かさ}ね{着|ぎ}: layering clothes — a noun describing the fashion or practice of wearing layers\n- {着|き}る: to wear, put on — basic verb for wearing; no implication of multiple layers\n- {羽織|はお}る: to throw on, drape over — putting on a single outer garment casually",
